fix(#62): add missing overlay visible state to ImageZoom CSS

[data-rmiz-modal-overlay] only had a `hidden` background-color, so the
modal backdrop never dimmed when zooming in. With no darkening cue
accompanying the (correctly) growing image, the zoom read as shrinking
rather than expanding — perceived as "zooming out."

transform-origin: 0 0 on [data-rmiz-modal-img] was reviewed and left
unchanged: it matches react-medium-image-zoom's own shipped default
(dist/styles.css uses the equivalent `top left`), and the library's
FLIP-style animation (translate/scale computed relative to the
thumbnail's top-left position) depends on that anchor to grow toward
the viewport center correctly. Changing it would misalign the
animation math rather than fix anything.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
